WEBVTT

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:14.029
All right, there we go.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:23.629
Okay, I'll just record so I have some record of what happened, and it will hopefully detect our voices and go to the bathroom, and then we will continue.

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:24.109
Okay.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.060
Roger Kyle used the illustration.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:09.859
Just go for the play.

00:03:02.189 --> 00:03:02.989
Oh, right, Daran.

00:03:03.309 --> 00:03:04.909
I like doing what's already there.

00:03:12.199 --> 00:03:13.719
Ooh, I have something for you.

00:06:14.219 --> 00:06:14.459
Here.

00:06:15.259 --> 00:06:16.539
I have next one, please.

00:06:18.139 --> 00:06:18.939
2014.

00:06:19.179 --> 00:06:19.819
The 2014.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.579
This is the one I wanted to give you.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.460
Oh, you can have them both.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:53.780
Actually.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:55.300
Are these different?

00:06:55.939 --> 00:06:56.259
Yes.

00:06:56.579 --> 00:06:58.740
So 2025 edition.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:06:59.220
Oh.

00:06:59.699 --> 00:07:01.220
5.5, 5.

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:01.540
Okay.

00:07:01.939 --> 00:07:02.180
Okay.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.699
Who governs these things?

00:07:05.939 --> 00:07:08.100
You know, the versions, the 5.5.5?

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.340
They're being called Hasbro and subdivision Wizards of the Coast.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.379
So Hasbro was the one who created the students in my life.

00:07:15.939 --> 00:07:16.100
No.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:19.830
I'm familiar with Hasbro.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.470
I used to buy a lot of things.

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:27.810
One second.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.170
Okay, no, it's only in here.

00:07:35.329 --> 00:07:35.569
Okay.

00:08:05.019 --> 00:08:05.740
So let's just, let's just.

00:08:06.139 --> 00:08:06.220
Yes.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:06.620
Okay.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:07.580
Yes, there is an app.

00:08:07.819 --> 00:08:08.860
Yeah, 1970s.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.460
Gary, Geigerx, and David.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:15.020
If you want to have the more fun version of it, search online.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.139
Search online?

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:16.379
Yes.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:16.699
Okay.

00:08:17.259 --> 00:08:20.939
And if you're really curious, it's a funny story.

00:08:21.259 --> 00:08:21.579
Okay.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:22.540
There you go.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:25.020
Okay.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:26.220
All right.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:27.500
So, yeah, so those are the books.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:28.379
Enjoy.

00:08:28.699 --> 00:08:29.020
Okay.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.020
I'll just take the latest one.

00:08:31.579 --> 00:08:32.220
Take both of them.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:33.980
They're collecting best and I think.

00:08:34.539 --> 00:08:36.300
Oh, you thought reading these?

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:40.539
I have them online and I have like copies of them.

00:08:40.779 --> 00:08:41.100
So.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:42.300
Sweet.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:45.580
Like, you're actually freeing space in my house.

00:08:45.899 --> 00:08:46.220
Okay.

00:08:47.899 --> 00:08:48.620
Happy friendship.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:50.539
How expensive do you?

00:08:50.779 --> 00:08:51.580
Yeah, no, yeah, no.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:58.139
I mean, if I, I will, I'll give you actually one more because like I the copy, they're occupying space in my garage, right?

00:08:58.460 --> 00:08:58.940
Right.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:00.379
I want it again.

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:16.629
And here's the monster.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:28.360
So here, like, this way you could learn all about monsters.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:32.520
I wouldn't recommend reading it because it's always fun to be surprised.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:37.720
But if you ever wanted to learn what goblins are really like, you could go read them.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:38.920
Right?

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.560
So the monster.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:46.840
Okay, the monster book manual is useful for the DM, right?

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.440
Yes, but I said, like I said, you made one of the.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:54.280
Oh, it helps the players to know.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.560
The goal is that, you know, the players.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:59.400
Players have fun, right?

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:05.320
I mean, the whole point of this game is it gives you the point is to tweak your imagination to have ideas.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:06.600
Correct, yes.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:09.800
All right, that is the intent of it, nothing else.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.240
Make sense?

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:12.280
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:15.410
Okay.

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:19.250
It's gotta be like time reading books.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:27.410
So, and by the way, if just so you know, I have given you access to my entire RPG library on the ND Beyond.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:31.250
Yeah, you should be able to access all of the books there.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:35.900
Go to rules.

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:39.630
Just click on any book.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:41.550
What are the books?

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.390
Pre-conferences for some reference document?

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:48.990
No, no, go to library.

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:51.710
View all.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:54.270
Click on that one.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:55.550
Sorry.

00:10:58.910 --> 00:10:59.230
Yeah.

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:00.110
Oh.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.070
These are all the ones that I purchased.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.070
This is shared with me, meaning anyone that's shared with me, you could read.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:08.030
Okay, okay.

00:11:10.910 --> 00:11:12.910
Well, I do have the monster in the clear.

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:13.470
Yeah, I know.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:16.350
I'm just, like, that's why I'm happy to give them to you.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:18.430
Right.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:19.870
I have it in digital.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:21.870
I have it in 10 digital formats.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:28.270
And so I've decided that I prefer now that I figured out how to use the digital formats in L1s.

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:32.990
Like certain manuals just don't inspire me.

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:36.670
Like I have fancy versions of those, which are like the special covers and whatnot.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:37.790
That I'm keeping.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.830
But just the fifth edition rules.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.630
I haven't opened one of those books in ages.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.630
Have you been to Grillhouse in San Jose?

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:47.470
No, you should go there.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:48.830
Yeah, I should go there.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:49.550
Right.

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:50.110
So, all right.

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:52.590
So let's just remind you of what happened last time.

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:58.830
We went into the crypts.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:11:59.390
Yeah.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:00.110
I have a summary.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:00.910
I have summaries.

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:01.790
Please.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.510
This is Costax, right?

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:06.270
We do not do things.

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:07.150
We are not.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:11.150
This is not a cheap campaign.

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.350
This is a high quality.

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:14.270
This is a high-class establishment.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:15.390
High-class.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:25.899
Right.

00:12:26.139 --> 00:12:33.180
The air in Tresendar Crypt was thick with the smell of ancient stone and decay as the party squared off against a cluster of skeletal guardians.

00:12:33.659 --> 00:12:44.540
One of the undead creatures raised a shortbow and loosed an arrow at the group, but the shot went wild, wild, missing spectacularly in the DM's world, claddling harmlessly against the far wall.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.820
Zenvon Foreput pressed forward and struck at the nearest skeleton.

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:54.779
His first swing missed, but a second connected with a natural 20, drawing first blood in the grim underground chamber.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:43.060
Three points to you can be total party, total party kill.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.420
Oh, a party kill.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:47.620
All right.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:58.420
With the frightened skeletons gone, the remaining undead fought on, and one of them landed a vicious blow against Zenvon, with its short sword dealing 11 points of damage and leaving him with only four points remaining.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:02.100
Pip Thistlewick, and Veyra coordinated their attacks with practical efficiency.

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:15.620
Pip cut down the skeleton he had already wounded and spent his action surge to strike down for six points, while Veyra, having already expended two prior castings of magic missile, used her last remaining slot here, the glowing darts picking apart bone and sinew.

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:22.020
Zenvon switched to a scimitar for Nick, missed his first swing, and landed the second for 12 points to destroy another.

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:27.860
With Zenvon backing away at four points, the last skeleton turned on Pip and instead caught him for six.

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:35.300
And it was Pip, not Zenvon, whom Sister Maela healed, laying her hands on him and channeling 10 points of divine restoration to the Cure Wounds.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:45.300
Zenvon closed the fight with his dagger, rolled a 24 to hit, and dealing eight points of damage before the party turned their attention to the three stone sarcophagi resting in the chamber.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:50.900
As they searched the ancient remains, the two skeletons that had fled earlier crept black into the room.

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:59.860
Upon noticing the red cloaks the party wore, however, the party's creatures simply stood at attention, recognizing the guards as a sign of allegiance and choosing not to attack.

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:06.340
The DM noted in a moment of candid rules correction that the skeleton should not have attacked the party to begin with and applied the detail very directly.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:17.300
Digging through the sarcophagus, Zenvon's fingers posed around a jeweled gold bracelet nestled among the bones of a human woman, a valuable find worth 140 gold pieces.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:18.740
It was then that the party heard it.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.900
Muffled cries drifting through the northeastern door.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:23.140
An investigation check confirmed what the voices were.

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:24.820
Please help us!

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:26.740
Desperate and frightened candidates.

00:15:27.220 --> 00:15:33.460
The cleric turned to Zenvon with a firm look and reminded him that they were the good guys, and the helpless, the helpless, deserved their protection.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:37.780
Zenvon related, I'll do this for you, Sister M, and the party moved towards the door.

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:42.820
When they pushed it open, they found a long room divided by iron bars into filthy cells lined with straw.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:45.300
The hinged doors secured by chains and padlocks.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:50.259
Two human women were locked in one cell, and a young boy was confined in another, all captives of the Redbrand.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:56.980
Before the party could act, however, a group of Redbrand ruffians who had been lying in wait lunged forward, attempting to catch the adventurers off guard.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:02.100
Their ambush failed entirely, the ruffians rolling so poorly that no one was caught by surprise, and the fight was on.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:10.500
Zenvon darted forward and drove his dagger into the nearest ruffian for five points before slipping out and using his cunning action to disengage.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:16.580
Sister Maela swung her hammer with righteous furry, cracking bone and sending one of the bandits reeling with six points of damage.

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:21.140
Pip cut down a wounded ruffian with a single decisive strike for six points, killing him outright.

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:26.580
Veyra unleashed a bolt of fire that scored eight points of damage and drove another to within a hit point of death.

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:29.540
This time, the DM allowed, the damage did sound the way it looked.

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:33.700
Sister Maela then called down a column of sacred radiant flame.

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:37.060
The ruffian blew his saving throw, took five points of damage, and died.

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:42.259
The last surviving ruffian, seeing his companions fall one by one, turned and bolted from the room.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:46.500
Pip gave chase while Zenvon and Sister Maela stayed to fear the prisoners.

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:48.019
Zenvon worked quickly.

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:49.620
Is it Zenvon or Zenvon?

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:51.620
All right.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:55.780
Quickly picking the locks on the iron bars with dexterity check, and the young boy burst free with delight.

00:16:55.940 --> 00:17:02.340
Sister Maela unlocked the remaining cell to release the captive women, but Pip's sprint after the fleeing bandit came to a sudden, painful halt.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:02.980
Halt.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:09.620
The floor gave way beneath his feet, and he plunged 20 feet into a hidden pit trap, landing hard in the darkness below.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:11.299
The DM rolled poorly for damage.

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.220
Pip survived, only with three points taken.

00:17:13.299 --> 00:17:14.980
Still, the bandit had gained precious ground.

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:19.220
Zenvon rushed to the edge of the pit and improvised, pressing his whip into service.

00:17:19.299 --> 00:17:21.700
As a makeshift rope, he pulled Pip up to safety.

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:27.380
Veyra attempted to catch the fleeing ruffian with a bolt of fire, but missed entirely, scorching the wall instead.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:31.460
Sister Maela mended Pip's injuries with another touch of design magic.

00:17:31.779 --> 00:17:34.420
Six more hit points were stored, and a party pushed on.

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:37.220
They entered a large cellar below the Tresendar Manor.

00:17:37.299 --> 00:17:39.460
A read aloud from the module described the space.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:45.860
A five-foot landing 10 feet above the cellar floor, stone steps ascending in two short flights, and a door beneath with stairs to the north.

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:50.980
A great cistern dominating the western wall and racks of kegs and barrels lining the room.

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:55.460
The party noted that the cistern did not noted the cistern, but did not search it yet.

00:17:56.160 --> 00:18:00.880
Investigation roll of 19 at the door of the upper landing revealed voices murmuring on the other side, several of them.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:04.480
The fleeing ruffian had clearly warned his companions.

00:18:04.799 --> 00:18:08.960
Zenvon considered his options for only a moment before a bold plan took shape.

00:18:09.119 --> 00:18:14.240
He threw open the door and stood and wore his red cloak, projecting the confidence of the man who belonged there.

00:18:14.559 --> 00:18:16.240
The bandits paused and looked at the cloak.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.359
Wait, you're one of us?

00:18:17.599 --> 00:18:18.960
They turned on their own comrade.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.480
What do you mean they attacked you, man?

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:22.799
Are you sure these guys are the guys that attacked you?

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:24.880
The ruffian jabbed back defiantly.

00:18:25.039 --> 00:18:27.039
Do I look like I'm the kind of person who would lie?

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:28.240
That is a killing machine.

00:18:28.319 --> 00:18:28.720
Kill him.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:34.480
But Zenvon seized the moment, pointing at the fleeing ruffian and accusing him of being a traitor who had let enemies into the high ground.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.759
We are one of you guys.

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:36.480
Look at this guy.

00:18:36.559 --> 00:18:37.759
This guy has turned the traitor.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:38.960
He was trying to let someone in.

00:18:39.119 --> 00:18:41.200
So that's what I wanted to catch him and eliminate him.

00:18:41.440 --> 00:18:43.279
The ruffian failed his counterpersuasion.

00:18:43.359 --> 00:18:48.400
One of the bandits named Dosarok immediately believed it and declared, About time somebody cleaned housed.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:50.319
I'm going to cut his rat into several pieces.

00:18:50.559 --> 00:18:53.039
A second, more skeptical bandit was not fully convinced.

00:18:53.359 --> 00:18:54.480
Hmm, traitor, funny.

00:18:54.559 --> 00:18:58.480
Nobody sent down word, but it's not very convincing when he's covered in blood and you're covered in blood.

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:00.559
He announced he would need to go verify the story.

00:19:00.799 --> 00:19:04.880
Zenvon offered to accompany him and lure him toward the waiting party on the stairs.

00:19:05.039 --> 00:19:11.039
The moment the skeptical bandit came within reach, Pip struck him for six points with his source, and the ruse unraveled in an instant.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:12.720
A chaotic brawl erupted.

00:19:12.799 --> 00:19:14.480
Pip finished the bandit he had struck.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:18.559
Zenvon drove his dagger home for 12 points of bandit of damage.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:25.599
When the dust settled, only a bandit named Wick was left standing beside the injured but still living Redbrand ruffian who had originally fled.

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:27.519
Wick made his calculation quickly.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:31.519
He cut down the wounded ruffian himself, then threw up his hands and begged for mercy.

00:19:31.839 --> 00:19:34.160
Wick was willing to talk, and Zenvon pressed him hard.

00:19:34.319 --> 00:19:38.160
The thug described Glasstaff as a dangerous wizard, not merely a figurehead.

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:40.799
I'd seen him drop a bandit, a spell, no weapon drawn.

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:42.319
Nobody messes with him twice.

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:50.079
He mentioned that the dungeon beneath the manor had multiple levels and that the subterranean depths were deeply unsettling in a way that went beyond ordinary danger.

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:53.359
There's something really wrong over there that messes with your head, I'm told.

00:19:53.599 --> 00:20:00.400
He added that Glasstaff answered to somebody that he had overheard the wizard complaining about orders from town references to the boss's business.

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:05.200
Someone in Phandalin, Wick believed, but the sentence trailed off before he could finish his thought.

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:12.720
With Zenvon spoke the name Black Spider visibly flinched, his face going pale, but when pressed, he retreated behind ignorance.

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:14.079
Look, dude, I just carry crates.

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:16.000
All right, you start asking about the boss's boss.

00:20:16.079 --> 00:20:18.400
That's how people end up caring less.

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:25.759
Under further duress, Wick offered one final piece of information: that the Redbrands had previously handled a family called the Dendrars.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:30.079
The DM confirmed quietly that this was the same family the party had just freed from themselves.

00:20:30.319 --> 00:20:31.680
Zenvon weighed his options.

00:20:31.759 --> 00:20:38.000
Wick had made a show of wanting to join the party in exchange for gold, and the high insult roll confirmed what Zenvon already suspected.

00:20:38.319 --> 00:20:39.119
The man was lying.

00:20:39.279 --> 00:20:41.519
He wanted the coin and the first opportunity to disappear.

00:20:41.839 --> 00:20:43.920
Not that he'll betray you, but that's what he wants to.

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:47.920
The DM noted, adding that Wick's, of course, I'm with you, boss, rang hollow.

00:20:48.079 --> 00:20:51.119
There was no loyalty to be bought, only a flug looking for an exit.

00:20:51.279 --> 00:20:54.400
Zenvon made his decision and let his end in the cellar.

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:58.000
Only then led the party turned to the cistern and the search paid.

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:06.559
A waterproof satchel hung from a submerged rope attached to the south wall about two feet below the water's surface, holding a potion of healing and a potion of invisibility.

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:19.839
They looted the fallen bandits as well, bodies carrying 16 silver and seven gold on one, twelve silver and five gold on another, and twenty copper pieces, electrum pieces, and two garnets with 10 gold pieces on each, each on the third.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:25.360
With the barracks cleared and the treasure secured, the party made their way to the cells where the three captives were still waiting.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:30.960
The two skeletal guardians from the crypts had drifted back to the doorway, standing passive in the presence of the red cloaks.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:36.400
On the other side, however, the captives had barricaded themselves in, terrified by the skeletons just outside.

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:38.720
Zenvon called out to them: Hey guys, it's me.

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:39.599
I came back for you.

00:21:39.759 --> 00:21:40.480
It's all safe now.

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:41.680
You can let go of the door.

00:21:41.759 --> 00:21:42.240
Let me help you.

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:46.400
The sound of the furniture scraping across stone followed, and then the door swung open.

